From 090f1f539aeeb7568bb87a586dfee839d83e6f91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 14:04:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 865/913] lib: libpng: fix uninitialized tRNS buffer, harden
 zTXt null-terminator
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

png_handle_tRNS: Initialize readbuf array to prevent use of an
uninitialized variable when processing non-PALETTE color types.

png_handle_zTXt: Guard the null-terminator write on the decompressed
buffer with a bounds check against the actual read buffer allocation
(read_buffer_size), rather than the unrelated chunk length, and report
a benign error if that bound is ever violated.

Coverity issue: CID 892682: Uninitialized scalar variable
Coverity issue: CID 1207391: CERT-C Expression

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git bf72c794129f90e1e4d222d0c66d871c0842da3f lib: libpng: fix uninitialized tRNS buffer, harden zTXt null-terminator]
Assisted-by: GitHub-Copilot:Claude-Sonnet-5
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Iaa3bbb1e37df80f617e6a1ec45b30e3059a8673a
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/592841
Domain-Review: Yannick FERTRE <yannick.fertre@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Philippe CORNU <philippe.cornu@foss.st.com>
---
 lib/libpng/pngrutil.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/libpng/pngrutil.c b/lib/libpng/pngrutil.c
index d5fa08c39..41a51d909 100644
--- a/lib/libpng/pngrutil.c
+++ b/lib/libpng/pngrutil.c
@@ -1816,7 +1816,7 @@ png_handle_sPLT(png_structrp png_ptr, png_inforp info_ptr, png_uint_32 length)
 void /* PRIVATE */
 png_handle_tRNS(png_structrp png_ptr, png_inforp info_ptr, png_uint_32 length)
 {
-   png_byte readbuf[PNG_MAX_PALETTE_LENGTH];
+   png_byte readbuf[PNG_MAX_PALETTE_LENGTH] = {0};
 
    png_debug(1, "in png_handle_tRNS");
 
@@ -2683,7 +2683,15 @@ png_handle_zTXt(png_structrp png_ptr, png_inforp info_ptr, png_uint_32 length)
              * it isn't necessarily '\0' terminated.
              */
             buffer = png_ptr->read_buffer;
-            buffer[uncompressed_length+(keyword_length+2)] = 0;
+            /* Bound against the actual allocation (read_buffer_size), not
+             * 'length', since read_buffer was resized by
+             * png_decompress_chunk(); this is the real overflow check.
+             */
+            if (uncompressed_length + (keyword_length+2) <
+                png_ptr->read_buffer_size)
+               buffer[uncompressed_length+(keyword_length+2)] = 0;
+            else
+               errmsg = "internal error: read buffer too small";
 
             text.compression = PNG_TEXT_COMPRESSION_zTXt;
             text.key = (png_charp)buffer;
-- 
